A||||2||Sillhouette.com||Has anyone tried this?||||1||
Z||000000||Sillhouette.com||07-21-2000||05:33 PM||||I was wondering what some of your with a five speed monzie and V6 get for a speed at 5500 RPM?   Is there anyone out there that can run the car at 6000 rpm?<P>Cheers||||reg||1
Z||000001||PJ||07-22-2000||10:53 AM||||It depends on your final drive ratio and the size of the tires. With the 3.65 final you'll never see 6,000 RPM in fifth. Especially with big rear tires. You might get close in fourth though. In fact with the 3.65 I hardly ever used fifth, it just slowed the car down. Maxes out at about 135MPH (its hard to tell, the speedo goes to 120MPH) and it takes a while to get there.<P>With the 3.95 final, redline in fourth is easy and its a lot quicker getting there. The car squirts out of the corners instead of bogging down. Fifth gear becomes a necessity. I usually run with the rev limiter set at 6,400RPM. I was able to go from 205/50's to 225/50's with the 3.95.<P>PJ<BR>ITA #66 Black<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||07-22-2000||11:09 AM||||At 120 mph my 5 speed does ~4200 rpm. I don't think the stock engine and stock gearing has enough horses to get up to 5500 rpm in 5th(160 mph) or 6000 rpm (170mph).<P>I've hit 60 mph (6000rpm) in 2nd..the rev limiter cuts in. That scared the he11 out of me the first time that happened.  I thought I blew the engine. I don't go there anymore.||||reg||1
